#### Challenge CQ-02 (`ASCII`) Verification
- **Input Array:** `[99, 114, 121, 112, 116, 111, 123, 65, 83, 67, 73, 73, 95, 112, 114, 49, 110, 116, 52, 98, 108, 51, 125]`
- **Decoded Output:** `crypto{ASCII_pr1nt4bl3}`

![CryptoHack ASCII Encoding Challenge Completed](../02-Cryptography/screenshots/Screenshot%202026-11-05%20091537.png)

#### Challenge CQ-03 (`You either know, XOR you don't`) Decryption Script & Output (`decod.py`)
```python
def xor_decrypt(hex_ciphertext, key_str):
    ciphertext = bytes.fromhex(hex_ciphertext)
    key = key_str.encode()
    decrypted = bytes([c ^ key[i % len(key)] for i, c in enumerate(ciphertext)])
    return decrypted.decode(errors='ignore')

hex_str = "0e0b213f26041e480b26217f27342e175d0e070a3c5b103e2526217f27342e175d0e077e263451150104"
secret_key = "myXORkey"

flag = xor_decrypt(hex_str, secret_key)
print(f"Flag: {flag}")
```

```text
(.venv) cyberflex@DESKTOP-CYBERFLEX:~/Desk$ python3 decod.py
Flag: crypto{1f_y0u_Kn0w_En0uGH_y0u_Kn0w_1t_4ll}
```

